messages.content:
@Vik Olliver any ideas about depositing/growing metal pillars from the head?
After say a zincate+nickel bath, we could then grow e.g. copper or silver pillars directly where they are wanted, and thus support bonding from them not just the plated surface-pattern-defined ones.
They'd also be raised naturally which would work great for ACF and should work as a self-stencil to pick up a coating of silver/copper sinter paste from a smooth pad that was coated thin in it, and thus allow pressing the die against a PCB/substrate (or other die!) to the do the sintering, while skipping the difficulty of depositing the paste thin and even to very small pads with just a traditional stencil (practical resolution) or syringe-nozzle (viscosity/particle size effects possibly clogging a nozzle).
